    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. On the screen reader side, what are some of the most common \"edge cases\" or little bugs that tend to pop up during testing that might mess up the experience for someone using assistive tech?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common edge cases include tab ordering issues, where screen readers Announce too quickly or abruptly between interactive elements. Another common issue is incorrect ARIA attributes or attributes not being applied to elements, causing screen readers to misinterpret their role or content. Additionally, missing or improperly implemented keyboard focus management can also cause difficulties for users relying on assistive tech.",
      "source": "target",
