    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, the ARIA stuff is always a headache. It feels like these little errors are just hiding in the code waiting to ruin everything. Do you have any advice on how to catch those sneaky, hard-to-find glitches before they actually hit the users?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can make use of browser DevTools' Accessibility panel to detect ARIA issues, automate testing with tools like axe or WAVE, and carefully observe screen reader interactions to identify potential issues. Another strategy is to write simple screenshots or printouts of the page for screen reader users, then review them closely to catch any ARIA-related errors. This hands-on, bottoms-up approach tends to reveal hidden errors more effectively.",
      "source": "target",
